        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45881</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45881"/>
        <updated>2026-09-28T23:46:05.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #23740.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="1537572591" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/23740" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/23740/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/23740">#23740</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Specifically I've tried to address</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Timing-Allow-Origin is needed for CORS and no-cors, it's for cross-origin protection</li>
<li>In the case of cross-origin iframes, responseEnd might measure when the iframe finished loading completely with all its subresources, not just the main resource.</li>
<li>encoded/decoded body size are  CORS-protected rather than TAO protected</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">The pages weren't to our templates, so some sections moved into a description.</p>
<p dir="auto"><a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/noamr/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/noamr">@noamr</a> Is this something you could review? I think I understood this, but I did use Claude a bit for confirmations and it can be deceptive.</p>]]></content>
