    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Add missing ReadOnlyInline to pages that already use them]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45873</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45873"/>
        <updated>2026-09-28T00:51:00.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">I don't know how dogmatic we are in enforcing that readonly properties are marked as readonly, but it's certainly a bug if a page is already using them and there exist readonly properties that aren't indicated as such, because then readers would assume that their absence means they are not readonly.</p>]]></content>
