    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Remove read-only modifiers from properties that are not]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45872</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45872"/>
        <updated>2026-09-28T09:33:46.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55398995?u=9f6a9837c9879eceb0abde487a338b92d4e206fc&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">It might be okay for read-only properties to not be marked as such (our guidelines are murky) but it's never okay for non-readonly properties to be marked as such.</p>
<p dir="auto">Namely:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>Dictionaries are never readonly (<code class="notranslate">MediaTrackSupportedConstraints</code>)</li>
<li>Derived class members are protocols and can never be enforced as readonly (<code class="notranslate">AudioWorkletProcessor.parameterDescriptors</code>)</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">...others are just typos. They have never been read-only.</p>]]></content>
        <author>
            <name>Josh-Cena</name>
            <email>Josh-Cena@noreply.github.com</email>
            <uri>https://github.com/Josh-Cena</uri>
        </author>
        <published>2026-09-28T00:40:42.000Z</published>
    </entry>
