        <title type="html"><![CDATA[CSS relative colors: explain channel values outside the output range]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45847</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/45847"/>
        <updated>2026-09-25T12:12:23.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143684587?u=5439f94a2cf31212e19f179d4defd1344c321579&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Adds a "Channel values outside the output range" subsection to the "Using relative colors" guide, with a worked <code class="notranslate">display-p3</code> example showing that channel values beyond the output function's range are used as they are, not clamped or gamut-mapped.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">The guide explains that channel values resolve to <code class="notranslate">&lt;number&gt;</code> values, but not what happens when the origin color lies outside the output function's gamut. Readers who compute <code class="notranslate">rgb()</code> relative colors from wide-gamut origins see values above <code class="notranslate">255</code>, and a <code class="notranslate">color(srgb ...)</code> serialization, with nothing on the page explaining either.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<p dir="auto">The example is the one <a class="user-mention notranslate" data-hovercard-type="user" data-hovercard-url="/users/romainmenke/hovercard" data-octo-click="hovercard-link-click" data-octo-dimensions="link_type:self" href="https://github.com/romainmenke">@romainmenke</a> suggested in the issue, kept inside the display-p3 gamut as recommended there. Values checked in Chromium 151:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">rgb(from color(display-p3 1 0.5 0.5) r g b)</code> computes to <code class="notranslate">color(srgb 1.07398 0.462581 0.483011)</code>, so <code class="notranslate">r</code> is about <code class="notranslate">273.86</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">rgb(from color(display-p3 1 0.5 0.5) calc(r - 1) g b)</code> computes to <code class="notranslate">color(srgb 1.07006 0.462581 0.483011)</code></li>
<li>the absolute <code class="notranslate">rgb(272.86 117.96 123.17)</code> computes to <code class="notranslate">rgb(255, 118, 123)<span class="ml-1 d-inline-block border circle color-border-subtle" style="background-color: rgb(255, 118, 123); height: 8px; width: 8px;"></span></code>, clamped</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Spec: <a href="https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-5/#relative-colors" rel="nofollow">CSS Color 5, relative color syntax</a>.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related issues and pull requests</h3>
<p dir="auto"><span class="issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se" aria-label="This pull request closes issue #32704.">Fixes</span> <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2189521620" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32704" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/32704/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32704">#32704</a><br>
Relates to <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="2107524745" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/32004" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/pull/32004/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/32004">#32004</a></p>]]></content>
